      "math_academy_id": "q-17382",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Given that $y=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2{e}^{x}$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=1.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{x}+2{e}^{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope  of the tangent at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{3}{x}+2{e}^{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1}+2{e}^{1} \\\\  & =3+2e\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
